  "worked_solution": "A function $g(x)$ is concave up over an interval $(a,b)$ if ${g}^{\u2033}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nOn the given graph of $y={g}^{\u2033}(x)$, we can see that ${g}^{\u2033}(x)>0$ on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-4),$ $(-2,0),$ and $(2,4).$ \n\nTherefore, the function $g(x)$ is concave up on the intervals \n\n$$\n(\\,-\\infty ,-4\\,),\\,(\\,-2,0\\,),\\,(\\,2,4\\,).\n$$",
